Third-party code in draco_decoder.wasm

draco_decoder.wasm is a WebAssembly (wasm32-wasip1) build of the mesh
decoder of Google Draco 1.5.7 (https://github.com/google/draco; copyright
Google Inc. and other contributors, per its AUTHORS file). It is compiled
from the unmodified Draco 1.5.7 sources plus the wrapper
tools/draco-wasm/draco_wasi.cc by tools/draco-wasm/build-draco-wasm.sh,
which pins and checksums every input.

Draco is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its license file
is LICENSE-draco in this directory, copied unchanged from the Draco 1.5.7
source tree; its last section covers a documentation script of the Draco
repository that is not part of the decoder. Draco ships no NOTICE file.

The module also links parts of the wasi-sdk 34 sysroot. wasi-sdk 34 is
built from wasi-libc at commit 2e6fb9d8ee0cdf9e431fbcabe8af3115de000a13 and
llvm-project at commit 895aa2c896ada719451be2e3673c83da8ddf1141 (clang
23.1.0-wasi-sdk). The link of the module (wasm-ld --trace, same output
checksum) takes these inputs from it:

- wasi-libc: crt1-reactor.o and 350 members of libc.a. They come from the
  musl part (libc-top-half/musl), the cloudlibc part
  (libc-bottom-half/cloudlibc), wasi-libc's own sources
  (libc-bottom-half/sources) and dlmalloc. emmalloc and fts are not linked.
- LLVM: 15 members of libc++.a, 10 of libc++abi.a and 18 of the compiler-rt
  builtins (libclang_rt.builtins.a), plus code of the libc++ headers.

Their license files, copied unchanged from those commits, are in licenses/:

- licenses/wasi-libc/LICENSE: how wasi-libc is licensed (Apache License 2.0
  with LLVM Exceptions, Apache License 2.0, or MIT) and the parts derived
  from other works.
- licenses/wasi-libc/LICENSE-APACHE-LLVM, LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT: the
  three licenses it names.
- licenses/wasi-libc/musl-COPYRIGHT: musl (libc-top-half/musl/COPYRIGHT,
  MIT).
- licenses/wasi-libc/cloudlibc-LICENSE: cloudlibc
  (libc-bottom-half/cloudlibc/LICENSE, BSD-2-Clause).
- licenses/wasi-libc/dlmalloc-NOTICE: dlmalloc's public domain (CC0)
  notice, quoted from dlmalloc/src/malloc.c.
- licenses/llvm/libcxx-LICENSE.TXT, libcxxabi-LICENSE.TXT,
  compiler-rt-LICENSE.TXT: libc++, libc++abi and compiler-rt (Apache
  License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions; older code also under the legacy
  University of Illinois/NCSA and MIT licenses), from libcxx/LICENSE.TXT,
  libcxxabi/LICENSE.TXT and compiler-rt/LICENSE.TXT.

internal/draco runs the module with wazero (github.com/tetratelabs/wazero
v1.12.0, Apache License, Version 2.0), a Go module dependency compiled into
the rodin3d-mcp binary; its license and NOTICE are in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt with the other Go modules. wazero's NOTICE file
reads:

    wazero
    Copyright 2020-2023 wazero authors
